WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.280
You know, one of the things I was thinking about&nbsp;
yesterday, as we saw the second impeachment of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:12.480
Donald Trump, is that for a guy who has been&nbsp;
focused on being a winner, winning, winning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.440
winning and wanting to be the alpha and wanting to&nbsp;
be the big dog and wanting to be respected in all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.880
of this stuff, there's really been no bigger loser&nbsp;
than Donald Trump from the standpoint of American&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.840
presidents and what he's done to his party and&nbsp;
what he's done to the country. Donald Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:34.000
as we mentioned earlier, has now been impeached&nbsp;
twice. No president has ever been impeached twice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.560
Donald Trump lost the popular vote&nbsp;
twice, something no president has done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.200
in more than 100 years. It has happened&nbsp;
before, but it's been more than 100 years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:49.440
Donald Trump's presidency oversaw the loss of&nbsp;
the House of Representatives for Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.960
in twenty eighteen, lost the House. Trump's&nbsp;
mishandling of the virus has been not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:01.280
historically disastrous, but it, combined&nbsp;
with his wackiness, led Republicans to lose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:07.520
the Senate in 2020. And it led to Trump losing&nbsp;
the presidential race and making himself a one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:16.400
term president. Trump has been widely banned from&nbsp;
social media for completely flouting the rules of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:23.920
those sorts of social media platforms. And in so&nbsp;
doing all of this, Donald Trump has also damaged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:30.080
his own businesses, possibly irreparably losing&nbsp;
contracts with the city of New York, many of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:36.000
businesses decimated, as we've discussed, and will&nbsp;
lead to investigations of Trump's businesses for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.560
possible financial wrongdoing. He has destroyed&nbsp;
the reputations of his children, his son in law,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:48.400
and so many of the people around him. Possibly&nbsp;
irreparably, and all of that talk that Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.720
always says, you know, no one's ever seen anything&nbsp;
like this, like nobody's ever seen before, we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:58.640
gotten used to that phrase. He's right. It's true.&nbsp;
Trump is right about that. But unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:04.960
the superlatives and unprecedented elements of&nbsp;
this presidency are all bad. And unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:12.320
a lot of the awakening that we're seeing didn't&nbsp;
happen sooner. A lot of the damage was done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.800
by the time this partial awakening happened. But&nbsp;
I think it's also important for us to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:22.400
that most Trump events have not abandoned Trump.&nbsp;
There's some good new polling data that came out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:25.600
I believe it was yesterday, maybe&nbsp;
this morning. I saw it this morning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:30.080
which shows that although 10 Republican members&nbsp;
of the House did vote to impeach Donald Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:36.720
although some senators are saying Trump should&nbsp;
go, Pat Toomey, for example, we've heard critical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.600
comments from Mitt Romney and some Republican&nbsp;
voters have abandoned Trump. By and large,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:49.600
Trump continues to be supported by the Republican&nbsp;
electorate and he continues to be seen as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:54.080
arguably the most dominant and important force&nbsp;
in the Republican Party. So the idea that on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.920
Wednesday at noon, Trump becomes irrelevant to&nbsp;
American politics or to the Republican Party,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.920
so far it doesn't appear to be that way. Yes,&nbsp;
members of the House and Senate of the Republican&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:08.480
Party will, as I have told you, start to distance.&nbsp;
They will go back to saying we've got to focus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.560
on debt and deficit and religious freedom and&nbsp;
lowering taxes and cutting regulations and all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.080
of this stuff. And they'll sort of pretend Trump&nbsp;
never happened or certainly that they weren't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:22.240
being supportive of it. But for now, the majority&nbsp;
of the Republican electorate is sticking with him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.560
and it's unclear whether there are going to be&nbsp;
consequences and accountability for everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:32.080
Donald Trump has done. Incredibly, we know that&nbsp;
Trump still thinks he did a great job. He has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:37.280
weaponized his narcissism, and that's exactly&nbsp;
why he still thinks he did a great job. He thinks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:42.160
none of this stuff is his fault. He believes he's&nbsp;
the best. When Trump says I'm the best president,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:46.160
I've done more than anybody else. He clearly&nbsp;
believes it. And it shouldn't be ignored&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:51.680
that despite all of the losing, Trump has gotten&nbsp;
things done permanently and all of them are bad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.680 --> 00:04:00.480
The judges, the court appointments, the that's&nbsp;
irreversible. They Trump will leave. They will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:05.200
stay continuing to damage the country. And much of&nbsp;
that is thanks to Mitch McConnell and many of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:13.120
very Republicans that are now distancing. They put&nbsp;
in Trump's just judges and justices and the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:18.880
lost with climate and the environment. There's no&nbsp;
way to get that back. That's irreversible. We can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:23.840
now try to do even more to make up for&nbsp;
it. But every lost day, we never get back.&nbsp;

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:32.400
But Trump's greatest act, or maybe better said his&nbsp;
strongest action to make America great or greater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:40.640
is only six days away, which is going to be Donald&nbsp;
Trump leaving office arguably as the biggest loser&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:46.640
to ever be the president of the United States.
We'll have more on this on our Instagram page&nbsp;&nbsp;

